{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-40887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the least-squares solution of $Ax=b$, where \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071086/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ccc60d69dd08c311625f4ceecf789c57e1c1ebd348a9f21dac24f4d63379501"} {"question" "q-40887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 15\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071086/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ccc60d69dd08c311625f4ceecf789c57e1c1ebd348a9f21dac24f4d63379501"} {"question" "q-40887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "edda5ea9539e588e535263dd2e2cb91d7e2ef42baf775b9d0202da49fd9a4f30"} {"question" "q-40887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071086/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ccc60d69dd08c311625f4ceecf789c57e1c1ebd348a9f21dac24f4d63379501"} {"question" "q-40887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{15}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{15} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071086/state.json" "file_sha256" "8ccc60d69dd08c311625f4ceecf789c57e1c1ebd348a9f21dac24f4d63379501"} {"question" "q-40887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:an